{# Nothing to show. Built to the same shape as the saved page's empty state:
   name the state, say what will fill it, and offer the one action that does.
   What this replaced was a single "not found" image, which told a visitor that
   something was missing without saying what, why, or what to do about it --
   and read as an error on a page that is working correctly.

   An empty cancelled page is good news, not a gap to be filled, so it is not
   sent to the search form the way an empty booking list is. #}
{% if tab == 'cancelled' %}
    <div class="text-center py-5">
        <i class="fas fa-circle-check empty-state__icon"></i>
        <h2 class="h4 mt-3">Nothing cancelled</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-4">
            Every trip you have booked is still on. Cancel one and it will be kept here.
        </p>
        <a href="/my/bookings" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Back to my bookings</a>
    </div>
{% else %}
    <div class="text-center py-5">
        <i class="fas fa-plane-departure empty-state__icon"></i>
        <h2 class="h4 mt-3">No bookings yet</h2>
        <p class="text-muted mb-4">
            Once you book a flight it will be listed here, with its reference and the full itinerary.
        </p>
        <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Search for flights</a>
    </div>
{% endif %}
